   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI_06">Seefeldstrasse 73</name> <hi rend="superscript">III</hi>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zurich</name> VIII: <name type="geo" key="G_CHE">Switzerland</name>
                            </addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear <name type="person" key="weav76">Miss Weaver</name>: At the risk of boring you I would suggest also that perhaps <name type="person" key="bosc78">Mr de Bosschère</name> (who wrote to <name type="person" key="poun85">Mr Pound</name> about <rs type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">my book</rs>) or <name type="person" key="ciol80">your Paris correspondent</name> might review it in some French journal. I think that <name type="person">Mr Jaffe</name> who forwarded you my MSS has some relation with the <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">
                            <hi rend="underline">Journal</hi> <hi rend="underline">de</hi> 
                                <choice>
                                    <sic>
                                    <hi rend="underline">Génève</hi>
                                </sic>
                                    <corr>
                                    <hi rend="underline">Genève</hi>
                                </corr>
                                </choice>
                        </seg>. A notice of it will appear shortly, I hear, in <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">
                            <name type="work">
                                <hi rend="underline">H</hi> <hi rend="underline">Εσπερια</hi>
                            </name>
                        </seg>, a Greek weekly journal published in London, 62 Oxford Street.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>        	With kind regards</salute>
                        <salute>                    	sincerely yours</salute>
                        <signed>                                	<name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1917-06-14">14/6/917</date>
                        </dateline> </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">A review by <name type="person">F. Guillermet</name>, “Les livres: ouvrage anglais”, appeared in <name type="work">Journal de Genève</name> (<date when="1917-12-31">31 December 1917</date>), 2.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">A review by JJ’s acquaintance <name type="person">Pavlos Phocas</name>, in <name type="work">Hesperia</name> (<date when="1917-06-29">29 June 1917</date>), is mentioned in <name type="work">LI</name> 107.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
